L76: ## 【48†Get information about the current route with ActivatedRoute】
L77: 【49†`ActivatedRoute`】 is a service from `@angular/router` that provides all the information associated with the current route.
L78: 
L79:     `import {【50†Component】, inject} from '@angular/core';
L80:     import {【49†ActivatedRoute】} from '@angular/router';
L81: 
L82:     @【50†Component】({
L83:       selector: 'app-product',
L84:     })
L85:     export class Product {
L86:       private activatedRoute = inject(【49†ActivatedRoute】);
L87: 
L88:       constructor() {
L89:         console.log(this.activatedRoute);
L90:       }
L91:     }`
L92: The 【49†`ActivatedRoute`】 can provide different information about the route. Some common properties include:
L93: Property  | Details
L94: --- | ---
L95: `url`  | An `Observable` of the route paths, represented as an array of 【51†`UrlSegment`】 objects for each part of the route path.
L96: `data`  | An `Observable` that contains the `data` object provided for the route. Also contains any resolved values from the resolve guard.
L97: `params`  | An `Observable` that contains the required and optional parameters specific to the route.
L98: `queryParams`  | An `Observable` that contains the query parameters available to all routes.
L99: `resources`  | An optional record of read-only 【52†`Resource`】 instances defined on or inherited by the route (requires 【53†`withRouterResources()`】).
L100: Check out the 【49†`ActivatedRoute` API docs】 for a complete list of what you can access with in the route.
L101: ## 【54†Understanding route snapshots】
L102: 
L103: Page navigations are events over time, and you can access the router state at a given time by retrieving a route snapshot.
L104: 
L105: Route snapshots contain essential information about the route, including its parameters, data, and child routes. In addition, snapshots are static and will not reflect future changes.
